---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Battery Storage Systems Thailand | Solar Batteries | JJ Com Solar Cell';
const description = 'Professional solar battery storage installation in Koh Chang, Thailand. Energy storage systems, lithium-ion phosphate batteries, and backup power for Thai homes and businesses. Free quote.';
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="website"
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Solar Battery Storage Systems",
    "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "Thailand" }
  }}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Services</span> / <span>Battery Storage</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-yellow/20 text-solar-yellow px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6">
        Serving Thailand Since 2016
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Battery Storage Systems</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Store excess solar energy for night use, backup power during outages, and true energy independence across Thailand.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">24/7</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Power available day and night</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">95%+</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Round-trip efficiency</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">10+</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Year battery lifespan</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Battery Product Image -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <div class="relative rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg bg-gray-100">
        <img 
          src="/images/battery-storage-hero.webp" 
          alt="Huawei ESM-48100B1 lithium iron phosphate solar battery with SOC indicators showing active charging status"
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
          loading="eager"
          width="1200"
          height="800"
        />
        <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/60 to-transparent p-6">
          <p class="text-white font-medium">Huawei ESM-48100B1 LiFePO4 Battery — 4.8kWh modular storage for Thai homes and businesses</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Solar Battery Storage Works</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Solar photovoltaic modules generate direct current (DC) electricity during daylight hours, but most Thai households consume the majority of power in the evening, after sunset. Without an energy storage system, excess daytime generation from your PV panels is either exported to the Provincial Electricity Authority (PEA) grid at unfavorable rates or simply wasted.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        A properly sized solar battery bank solves this mismatch through a time-shift strategy. During daylight, your solar arrays feed DC power to a hybrid inverter equipped with Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) charge controllers. The inverter converts DC to alternating current (AC) for immediate household use, while surplus energy routes to your battery bank at optimal charging voltage. Modern lithium-ion phosphate (LiFePO4) batteries achieve 80% to 95% round-trip efficiency, meaning very little energy is lost in the storage cycle compared to older lead-acid technologies that typically achieve only 70% to 80%.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        When grid power fails, common during monsoon storms on Koh Chang and other Thai islands, the inverter automatically disconnects from the utility and switches to stand-alone mode within 10 to 20 milliseconds. This is fast enough that computers, medical equipment, and refrigeration continue operating without interruption. The battery management system (BMS) monitors each cell's state of charge, temperature, and depth of discharge. We typically configure residential systems to limit depth of discharge to 90% of rated capacity, preserving the 10% buffer that extends battery lifespan beyond 6,000 cycles, roughly 15 to 20 years of daily use in Thailand.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Battery Options We Install</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Lithium-Ion (Li-ion)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">High energy density, compact footprint, and fast charging capability. Best for urban homes and businesses with limited installation space. Typical configurations range from 5 to 15 kilowatt-hours of usable capacity. Suitable for properties where roof space is restricted but energy demand is moderate to high.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">LiFePO4 (Lithium Iron Phosphate)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Superior thermal stability and longer cycle life compared to standard lithium-ion. Ideal for Thailand's tropical climate where ambient temperatures regularly exceed 35 degrees Celsius. These solar batteries tolerate high humidity and resist thermal runaway, making them the safest choice for residential and commercial installations in coastal and island environments like Koh Chang.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why Battery Storage Matters in Thailand</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Thailand's electricity tariffs operate on a progressive scale, the more you consume, the higher your per-unit rate. For households consuming over 150 kWh monthly, rates climb to 4.0 to 5.5 THB per unit. By storing solar energy generated during peak sun hours and discharging it during evening peak pricing, you avoid the highest tariff tiers entirely.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Island communities face additional challenges. Koh Chang and similar destinations experience grid outages during monsoon season (May through October) when storms damage overhead lines. For resorts that cannot afford refrigeration downtime, family homes with medical equipment, or commercial facilities processing payments, battery backup ensures continuous operation. The combination of solar arrays and energy storage transforms your property from a passive consumer into an active, resilient power station.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Off-grid configurations common on remote Koh Chang properties use the battery as the primary energy reservoir, sized to provide 2 to 3 days of autonomy during monsoon season when heavy cloud cover reduces solar generation by 60% to 80%. We calculate autonomy requirements based on your critical load profile, the minimum equipment that must remain operational during extended bad weather.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What You Get with Our Battery Storage Service</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Professional assessment:</strong> We analyse your electricity bills, consumption patterns, and critical loads to specify the optimal battery capacity, typically 5 to 20 kilowatt-hours for residential systems.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Hybrid inverter integration:</strong> We supply and install inverters that manage both solar arrays and battery banks, with built-in MPPT charge controllers and automatic grid-islanding protection.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Safe installation:</strong> Batteries are mounted in ventilated, weatherproof enclosures with fire-resistant backing. All DC cabling uses appropriate gauge and fuse protection per Thai electrical standards.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>System programming:</strong> We configure charging schedules, discharge limits, and backup priorities. The BMS is calibrated for Thailand's voltage and frequency standards (220V, 50Hz).</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Monitoring setup:</strong> Smartphone app integration so you can track state of charge, daily cycles, and energy flows in real time from anywhere.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>1-year maintenance included:</strong> Annual capacity testing, BMS firmware updates, terminal cleaning, and thermal inspection at no additional cost.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Benefits of Solar Battery Storage</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Energy Independence</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Reduce reliance on the grid and rising PEA electricity tariffs. Generate, store, and consume your own power.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Backup Power</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Keep lights, refrigeration, medical equipment, and security systems running during grid outages.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Maximize Solar ROI</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Store daytime surplus for evening use instead of exporting at low net metering rates or wasting generation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Off-Grid Capability</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Complete energy autonomy for remote locations where grid connection is unreliable or unavailable.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Size your system with battery storage included</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-panels-cloudy-days/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Cloudy Day Performance</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">How batteries help during low-generation periods</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Ready for Energy Independence?</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Get a free battery storage assessment and personalised quote for your property in Thailand.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Get a Free Quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
